<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - Hungary T-bill, bond yields seen falling. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Hungary T-bill, bond yields seen falling. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields on Hungary's government securities are expected to continue declining at this week's auctions, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yields at the auction of seven-year bonds, which has floating interest fixed to the consumer price index, are also likely to drop. However, dealers declined to predict yield levels because market liquidity could change significantly before the auction.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management Agency will auction one-month discount Treasury bills on Tuesday, three-month bills on Wednesday, two-year bonds of the 1999/D series and seven years bonds of the 2003/F series on Thursday.</p>
